; Amarchy welcome and help text. One source: tools/gen_amarchy_help.py turns it into build/amiga/amhelp.inc (the
; welcome window and the Help view) and into the GETTING STARTED section of man/amarchy.1.
; Placeholders are filled from the live keymap: {key:ACTION} is the key bound to an action, {menu:ID} a menu path.
; A line may not start with an opening square bracket (that starts a section). Keep lines under 72 characters.

[welcome]
Amarchy puts the whole Amiga under one key, called Super.
Super is the Left Amiga key.

Open the menu:      {key:menu:root}
Snap a window left: {key:win:snap left}
Take a screenshot:  {key:cap:region}
Change the theme:   {menu:style.theme}
Open this help:     {key:gui:help}
Quit Amarchy:       {key:amarchy:quit}

The menu lists every program, setting and action. Press Escape
to close it. Every key above can be changed in the keymap file,
and this text then shows your key.

Tick the box below to stop this window from opening at start.

[help]
THE MENU
Press {key:menu:root} to open the menu. Use the arrow keys and Return, or
the mouse. Escape closes a level. Apps open with {key:menu:apps}. The
list of every key is on {key:viewer}.

WINDOWS AND TILING
Windows can be snapped to a half or a corner of the screen. Snap
left with {key:win:snap left} and right with {key:win:snap right}. Snap to the
top left corner with {key:win:snap tl}. Centre a window with {key:win:snap center}.
Bring a window to the front with {key:win:front}, zoom or restore it
with {key:win:zip}. Save its position and size with {key:win:save}.

THEMES
Choose {menu:style.theme} from the menu to change the look of the
whole desktop: colours, pointer, fonts and backdrop. The change
applies at once and is kept for the next start.

SCREEN CAPTURE
{key:cap:region} saves a dragged region, {key:cap:screen} the whole screen and
{key:cap:window} the active window. The picture is stored in
RAM:Shots as an IFF file and also placed on the clipboard.

THE STATUS BAR
The bar at the top of the screen shows the clock, memory and other
segments. Its rows are set in ENVARC:Amarchy/bar.conf.

PREFERENCES
Amarchy settings are in the menu under Settings. They are kept in
ENV:Amarchy and ENVARC:Amarchy.

THE KEYMAP FILE
Every key is a line in ENVARC:up-term/keymap. Put your own lines
in ENVARC:up-term/keymap.user so an Install does not replace
them. Then reload the keys from the menu or with the ARexx
command RELOAD.

AREXX
The port AMARCHY takes STATUS, RELOAD, RUN, SHOW and QUIT. The
manual page lists every command: read it with man amarchy.

QUITTING
Quit Amarchy with {key:amarchy:quit}. Its keys stop working until you
start it again.
